# Read-only corpus extraction output — real SOP titles and paths (firm-confidential)
corpus-analysis/

# Scratch space for the weekly-digest pipeline (timeline fetch, split script)
.scratch/

# Agent session state (snapshots, token logs, run markers) — tooling
# artifacts, never source. The leading **/ is required: a gitignore pattern
# containing an internal slash is anchored to the repo root, so a bare
# `.claude/sessions/` misses nested copies like apps/teams-bot/.claude/sessions/.
#
# Re-added 2026-09-12: PR #65 introduced this rule and the merge resolution of
# PR #66 dropped it while resolving a conflict on the line below. If it goes
# missing again, check the most recent .gitignore conflict resolution.
**/.claude/sessions/

# Token-optimizer state. `.token-optimizer/wiki/` ships its own `*` ignore —
# the tool's default is that its findings are unreviewed agent output and stay
# out of git. That directory is also ~7MB and holds full session transcripts,
# which must not enter the history of a repo handling tax return information.
# What the wiki rule leaves exposed is `authored/` — machine-local cache of no
# value to anyone else. Ignore the lot.
#
# `.serena/` is deliberately NOT here: it is committed. Serena's own
# `.serena/.gitignore` already excludes its cache and local-only config, so
# only the shared project config is tracked.
.token-optimizer/

# eval:gold reports contain real knowledge-base answers
gold-*.json

# P0 gate #1 content-audit worksheets contain document titles and SharePoint
# paths. The TRI scanner screens document bodies, not titles or folder names —
# whether those carry client-identifying material is the human judgment gate #1
# exists to make. Same reasoning as gold-*.json above. Generator:
# scripts/gate1-content-audit.mjs (it refuses to write to a tracked path).
gate1-audit-*.md
